Decide whether one current proposed identity refers to the same subject as an unresolved identity proposal from an
earlier consolidation run.

An unresolved identity proposal is a possible subject that is waiting for user review and is not part of the canonical
entity registry. Return `same_as_pending` when the current evidence establishes the same subject as exactly one prior
proposal. Return `distinct` when it establishes a separate subject. Return `review_required` when more than one result
remains plausible, citing the exact candidate proposal IDs.

Names alone are not sufficient when different subjects could share them. Use the defining context and supporting
evidence. This step only associates identity evidence; it does not approve a proposal, create an entity, decide its
type or visibility, or assign claim ownership. Return one schema-valid decision.
